---
description: Each Kotlin top-level type lives in its own file
globs: app/src/main/java/**/*.kt
alwaysApply: false
---

# One top-level type per file

- Do not group multiple unrelated top-level types in a single Kotlin file.
- Default convention:
  - One `data class` / `class` / `interface` / `enum` per file.
  - Name the file after the primary type (e.g. `UninstallResultsUiState.kt`, `UninstallResultItem.kt`, `UninstallResultStatus.kt` when split further).
- Small helper types that are tightly coupled (e.g. a private extension or nested sealed subclass) should prefer **being nested** inside the main type rather than declared as separate top-level types in the same file.

